.TH TOUCH 1
.SH NAME
touch \- create a file, or set its time to now
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B touch
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B touch
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
A
.I file
that does not exist is created, empty (mode 0644); one that exists keeps
its contents and gets the time now as its time of last change.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on the first failure (or without a name).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stat (1),
.BR sh (1)
